      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PEARLS IN JUNE (4) is the one to beat after returning with a decisive maiden win at Eagle Farm then placing in stronger company at the same venue. She was bumped last start, was still solid through the line, and looks well placed third-up despite having two unplaced tries around 1400m. CHIEF OF STAFF (3) is the main threat after missing by a length first-up at Lismore, where he began awkwardly and covered ground as a well-supported favourite. Kinder draw and fitness give him scope to improve. SORRENTI (2) was wide throughout at Eagle Farm after winning a maiden at Coffs Harbour and is credible back from mid-week company. COPPER STAR (5) keeps placing, draws barrier one, and brings reliable benchmark form, though this is his first look at 1400m. WILDSPITZE (8) has patchy form but there are efforts in there that can measure up. Keeping safe in exotics on quick turnaround.",
